From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:29:37 -0500
Subject: feat: the command bar's search folds case in any script and takes a
 Space's whole name (S-158, S-164)

docs/features/commandbar.md K2, K10, K19. The bar's title and keyword
matching folded ASCII alone, so a Cyrillic or accented title typed in
another case was not found. Both now fold case in any script.
"@Work Stuff rust" filtered to Spaces whose name starts with "Work" and
searched for "Stuff rust": a Space named in several words could not be
chosen. The longest whole name the text starts with, followed by a space
or the end, is now the filter, and it matches that Space alone;
otherwise the first word stays a prefix, folded the same way.

A patch of its own: the lines it changes belong to four earlier patches
(the bar's first, its keywords, the Spaces' query and the essentials'
filter), and both are extensions of those rows, not defects in them.

Why: Spaces are often named in more than one word, and titles in many
scripts; the command bar is how people leaving Arc find a tab.
Removable when: never; Stedding's own command bar.
